Worth me sending a quick example so you can see the output?","Hi Shahbaz, it's [name] - I know I'm calling out of the blue, do you have twenty seconds? I'll be quick. I saw Halo won the NACFB Cashflow award two years running and you're quoting same-day decisions across a big lender panel, so I just had one question about how the doc side keeps up with that.","Hi Shahbaz, it's [name] - calling about the document-intake side of keeping those same-day decisions moving across your lender panel. No pitch, just one idea worth comparing notes on - I'll drop you a short note too, or grab me back on [number].","Hi Shahbaz - [name] here, congrats on the back-to-back NACFB win. Quick one on keeping borrower docs moving fast enough for those same-day decisions - ok if I send a short example?","One thing I left out: the part brokers usually feel most is the borrower chase. The missing-doc follow-ups go out automatically, so the deal keeps moving even when you're heads-down on the next one. Happy to show how that piece works on its own.","Different angle - the bit that matters with a 130+ panel is re-cutting the same file to each lender's spec. That's the manual step we remove, so a deal you'd send to three lenders gets three clean packages without three rounds of admin. Worth a quick look?","We've already got our process dialled in - it's how we hit same-day, and the team knows it.","Totally fair, and I'd not touch the credit judgement or lender relationships - that's the bit that won you the award. This only sits on the intake step: borrower upload to sorted, flagged, lender-ready package, with the chase handled. If your process is already tight it just gives that step back time on the busy days. Happy to send one example and you can tell me if it'd even fit.","Person and company confirmed: Shahbaz Khan is a finance broker / lending specialist at Halo Corporate Finance, Milton Keynes (shahbaz@hcfl.co.uk, LinkedIn /in/skhangb) — identity is real and tied to the recorded lead. | 